From: OpenWrt-Spacemit-K1 project
Subject: [PATCH v2] riscv: dts: spacemit: enable AP6256 SDIO WiFi on OrangePi RV2

Hand-adapted for dhewg/openwrt's spacemit PR #23231 tree, NOT dgshue's own
devicetree backport. Hardware facts (pin numbers, IRQ 100, GPIO 67/116,
CLK_SDH1/RESET_SDH1) originate from https://github.com/dgshue/OpenWrt-RISC's
reverse-engineering; every insertion point and reference was independently
verified against dhewg's actual current tree.

v1 of this patch booted and crashed with a NULL pointer dereference in
pinctrl_commit_state, during a deferred-probe retry of the new SDIO
controller — traced to spacemit_sdhci_start_signal_voltage_switch
unconditionally looking up a "uhs"-named pinctrl state that v1 never
declared (only a single "default" state was given). Fixed in v2 by adding
a second mmc2_uhs_cfg pin group and pinctrl-1, mirroring the exact pattern
already working for this tree's own SD card slot (sdhci0). Also restored
no-mmc/no-sd on the WiFi slot, present in dgshue's original but dropped in
v1's adaptation.

Cross-referenced against Armbian's own build config for this board
(armbian/build, config/boards/orangepirv2.csc), which disables
CONFIG_MMC_UHS_SUPPORT kernel-wide as "disable MMC UHS support to speed up
MMC under Linux" — confirming UHS voltage-switching on this SoC is broadly
fragile, not a one-off bug in this patch specifically. A kernel-wide
disable was deliberately NOT copied here, since it would regress dhewg's
SD card slot, which already has full working UHS support in the clean
build. This fix is scoped to the WiFi slot only.

Verified before use:
  - dry-run and real patch apply against a fresh reconstruction of dhewg's
    actual tree (all 137 of his patches applied against the real pinned
    6.18.44 kernel source): clean, no fuzz, no rejects
  - cpp preprocess: clean
  - dtc compile to a real .dtb: clean, zero warnings

Still unverified: real hardware boot with v2's fix applied. v1's specific
crash is understood and addressed; this does not guarantee no further
issues exist. Must be paired with dgshue's patches 0005 (sdhci-of-k1
unaligned HOST_CONTROL2 panic fix) and 0006 (PMIC 32KOUT/RTC enable) — both
apply cleanly as-is.

diff -ruN dhewg_build/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1-orangepi-rv2.dts dhewg_build_modified/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1-orangepi-rv2.dts
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1-orangepi-rv2.dts	2026-08-31 16:15:02.434717590 +0000
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1-orangepi-rv2.dts	2026-09-01 22:33:16.686109625 +0000
@@ -20,12 +20,18 @@
 		ethernet1 = &eth1;
 		mmc0 = &emmc;
 		mmc1 = &sdhci0;
+		mmc2 = &sdhci1;
 	};
 
 	chosen {
 		stdout-path = "serial0";
 	};
 
+	wifi_pwrseq: wifi-pwrseq {
+		compatible = "mmc-pwrseq-simple";
+		reset-gpios = <&gpio K1_GPIO(67) GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	};
+
 	pcie_vcc3v3: regulator-pcie-vcc3v3 {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		enable-active-high;
@@ -417,3 +423,25 @@
 	sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&sdhci1 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default", "uhs";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&mmc2_cfg>;
+	pinctrl-1 = <&mmc2_uhs_cfg>;
+	bus-width = <4>;
+	non-removable;
+	no-mmc;
+	no-sd;
+	mmc-pwrseq = <&wifi_pwrseq>;
+	vmmc-supply = <&pcie_vcc3v3>;
+	vqmmc-supply = <&buck3_1v8>;
+	keep-power-in-suspend;
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <0>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	brcmf: wifi@1 {
+		compatible = "brcm,bcm43456-fmac", "brcm,bcm4329-fmac";
+		reg = <1>;
+	};
+};
diff -ruN dhewg_build/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1-pinctrl.dtsi dhewg_build_modified/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1-pinctrl.dtsi
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1-pinctrl.dtsi	2026-08-31 16:15:02.406175349 +0000
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1-pinctrl.dtsi	2026-09-01 22:33:07.982088214 +0000
@@ -646,4 +646,44 @@
 			power-source = <1800>;
 		};
 	};
+
+	mmc2_cfg: mmc2-cfg {
+		mmc2-data-cmd-pins {
+			pinmux = <K1_PADCONF(15, 1)>,   /* mmc2_d3 */
+				 <K1_PADCONF(16, 1)>,   /* mmc2_d2 */
+				 <K1_PADCONF(17, 1)>,   /* mmc2_d1 */
+				 <K1_PADCONF(18, 1)>,   /* mmc2_d0 */
+				 <K1_PADCONF(19, 1)>;   /* mmc2_cmd */
+			bias-pull-up = <0>;
+			drive-strength = <32>;
+			power-source = <1800>;
+		};
+
+		mmc2-clk-pins {
+			pinmux = <K1_PADCONF(20, 1)>;   /* mmc2_clk */
+			bias-pull-up = <0>;
+			drive-strength = <32>;
+			power-source = <1800>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	mmc2_uhs_cfg: mmc2-uhs-cfg {
+		mmc2-data-cmd-pins {
+			pinmux = <K1_PADCONF(15, 1)>,   /* mmc2_d3 */
+				 <K1_PADCONF(16, 1)>,   /* mmc2_d2 */
+				 <K1_PADCONF(17, 1)>,   /* mmc2_d1 */
+				 <K1_PADCONF(18, 1)>,   /* mmc2_d0 */
+				 <K1_PADCONF(19, 1)>;   /* mmc2_cmd */
+			bias-pull-up = <0>;
+			drive-strength = <32>;
+			power-source = <1800>;
+		};
+
+		mmc2-clk-pins {
+			pinmux = <K1_PADCONF(20, 1)>;   /* mmc2_clk */
+			bias-pull-up = <0>;
+			drive-strength = <32>;
+			power-source = <1800>;
+		};
+	};
 };
diff -ruN dhewg_build/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1.dtsi dhewg_build_modified/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1.dtsi
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1.dtsi	2026-08-31 16:15:02.399587217 +0000
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k1.dtsi	2026-08-31 22:15:13.018218800 +0000
@@ -1336,6 +1336,19 @@
 				status = "disabled";
 			};
 
+			sdhci1: mmc@d4280800 {
+				compatible = "spacemit,k1-sdhci";
+				reg = <0x0 0xd4280800 0x0 0x200>;
+				clocks = <&syscon_apmu CLK_SDH_AXI>,
+					 <&syscon_apmu CLK_SDH1>;
+				clock-names = "core", "io";
+				resets = <&syscon_apmu RESET_SDH_AXI>,
+					 <&syscon_apmu RESET_SDH1>;
+				reset-names = "axi", "sdh";
+				interrupts = <100>;
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
+
 			emmc: mmc@d4281000 {
 				compatible = "spacemit,k1-sdhci";
 				reg = <0x0 0xd4281000 0x0 0x200>;
